  "youtube": {
    "title": "Do This 10 Minutes Before Any Exam #shorts",
    "description": "Mind full of \"what if I blank?\" right before a test? Worry doesn't just feel bad: it eats up the working memory you need to answer questions.\n\nIn a classroom study, students wrote about their worries for 10 minutes right before a big exam. The most anxious students scored nearly a grade higher than anxious students who just sat quietly.\n\nNext exam: grab a page, write every worry down, then walk in lighter.\n\nResearch: Ramirez & Beilock (2011), \"Writing About Testing Worries Boosts Exam Performance in the Classroom\", Science.\n\n#shorts #exam #studytips #anxiety #psychology #animation #students",
